                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "79e363ba-9a97-332b-ae05-fc38e4aa806f",
                        "entry_id": "b8d02787-b971-3857-a63f-ec6c2ac479b1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To wind (tighten a spring of) something excessively."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fc5cc83f-b1f1-4af2-8975-5ac71c597741",
                                "sense_id": "79e363ba-9a97-332b-ae05-fc38e4aa806f",
                                "text": "People also come in full of misgivings about \"overwinding\" their watches. \"You can't overwind a watch - you can only underwind it,\" said McKelvey."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0448ef93-8fa1-4c38-b652-109ba08c21e6",
                                "sense_id": "79e363ba-9a97-332b-ae05-fc38e4aa806f",
                                "text": "In a typical Morris cock-snook at classical technique, tutu-ed dancers prance Bambi-like across the stage. On and off, on and off, with fixed smiles like overwound clockwork dolls: it should have been charming and funny, but despite stylish individual efforts, the ragged ensemble meant the joke fell flat."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "05b887f9-6e69-4d1d-b63c-3f2d2af04fab",
                                "sense_id": "79e363ba-9a97-332b-ae05-fc38e4aa806f",
                                "text": "I met him 10 years ago in a hallway in Harrisburg and departed with the image of a man whose psyche approximated a badly overwound clock: Everything is tight and in place, but nothing's moving."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7ff43752-0037-3ba0-8669-e6106619fd32",
                        "entry_id": "b8d02787-b971-3857-a63f-ec6c2ac479b1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To twist (itself) more tightly."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "570e80bb-0465-4eba-9975-2dfec10fc981",
                                "sense_id": "7ff43752-0037-3ba0-8669-e6106619fd32",
                                "text": "DNA's helical structure implies that twisting and stretching should be coupled, hence the prediction that DNA should unwind when stretched […] That is why it was such surprise when we directly measured twist-stretch coupling to find instead DNA overwinds when stretched."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
